{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"in-person-guides-custom-prompts","reason":"Full independent review completed. The recomputed SHA-256 matches the trusted order and the complete 193-line pinned raw was read. The accepted receipt, candidate and suggestions agree apart from the ordinary trailing-newline rendering difference, no format-repair artifacts are present, all five selected quotes are exact at their stated raw lines, the detail locators resolve, and the source metadata, canonical URL and raw provenance match the trusted order. The source otherwise accurately retains the five prompt families, mutation/context polling pattern, prompt-specific firmware or version statements, explicit enablement notes for multiple-choice, text and amount, multiple-choice limit, signature and confirmation result forms, conditional cancellation routes, waitForNextRequest timeout, offline exclusion, text/amount result retention and first-retrieval deletion, and sub-processor navigation boundary. Two scope errors remain: the final key takeaway says all other described text input types use the number pad even though SENSITIVE_ALPHANUMERIC displays a virtual keyboard, and the proposed concept generalizes environment enablement to the suite although the raw explicitly states Sandbox and Production enablement only for multiple-choice, text and amount. The proposed Custom Prompts concept addresses a genuine specialized topic gap; its narrow route is compatible with the parallel broader braintree-in-person proposal, and the coordinator can resolve whether to retain or consolidate that target without another topic inventory. The blocker-completeness pass found no other material false claim, missing warning, broken required route or undiscoverable central topic; routine parameters and examples appropriately remain in raw."}
